---

## 14. Development Lessons From the Project

### Build for the business, not for the résumé

The most useful features are not necessarily the most technically complex ones. The cart, dynamic menu, WhatsApp ordering and availability controls have direct operational value.

### Small local businesses can use custom software without a giant stack

Supabase + a lightweight frontend + Vercel + WhatsApp is enough to create a functional digital product for the current use-case.

### Features should support measurable behavior

The mystery reward exists to encourage the customer to cross a spending threshold. Reviews exist to create social proof. Search/categories exist to shorten menu discovery.

### Real usage exposes better requirements

The website evolved because actual business behavior revealed what mattered. That is stronger evidence than designing every feature up front.

